			<key>cell</key>
			<string>PSGroupCell</string>
			<key>footerText</key>
			<string>How far the view subtree walk goes, where it aims, and how often it runs. Focus restarts the depth budget at any view whose class name contains the text — it matches VIEW classes, not controllers, so “NowPlaying” never matches. Real ones here: TintColorObserving (the full-screen player's content root), Palette, DetailHeader. A node stopped by the depth cap is marked with how many children it did not visit.

Repeat scan exists because the two scans at 5s and 12s after launch cannot catch a screen you navigate to afterwards — three attempts at the full-screen player all dumped whatever was up at 12 seconds instead. Set it, open the screen you care about, and wait one interval. It stops after 40 scans.

For the artwork background: Depth 8, Max nodes 200, Focus TintColorObserving, Repeat every 10s, then open the full-screen player and wait.</string>
			<key>label</key>
			<string>Deep Dive</string>
